<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zliten Mosaic</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zliten Mosaic is a Roman floor mosaic found at a villa at Zliten, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leptis-magna">Leptis Magna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, depicting gladiatorial combat and the killing of prisoners by wild animals in the arena. It shows lions and leopards supplied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantes</a> being used in Roman arenas. It illustrates the trans-Saharan trade in exotic animals that linked the Garamantes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zliten-mosaic.jpg" alt="Zliten Mosaic" width="292" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bestiarii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Zliten Mosaic</b> near Leptis Magna, which appears to show captives, possibly Garamantes, thrown to wild beasts in the arena, reflects how closely Roman Tripolitania watched this frontier.</blockquote><a href="/empire/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
